  "panels": [
    {
      "grid": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 48,
        "h": 20
      },
      "config": {
        "title": "Pattern A / B and query methods",
        "content": "Line charts plot **successful runs only**. A series that stops is a 429 (or missing size), not a speedup.\n\n**Filter:** use the `test_id` control (this dashboard is set to `2026-08-29-a10k`). The original ingest is `2026-08-29`.\n\n## What these series mean\n\nTwo axes: **data shape** (A vs B) and **algorithm** (VALUES zip / TOP zip / search_after).\n\n### Pattern A vs Pattern B\n\nSynthetic `.rule-events` for one `episode.id`, 1-minute rule interval.\n\n| | Pattern A | Pattern B |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Flap style | all-flip | longer runs |\n| `run_len` | 1 | typically 10 |\n| Relationship | flaps = docs | flaps \u2248 docs / 10 |\n| Example | 1000 docs \u2192 1000 spans | 1000 docs \u2192 ~100 spans |\n| Stresses | every row is a status change | same window, fewer spans |\n\nSame `docs` = same 1m-rule window. A is worst-case flapping; B is closer to real episodes with stable runs.\n\n### VALUES zip vs TOP zip vs search_after\n\nHow spans are derived (not different data).\n\n| Method | Where | Returns | Cost |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **VALUES zip** | ES\\|QL in ES | full span geometry: start, end, `duration_ms`, `data` | pack rows into `VALUES()`, `MV_ZIP` twice, expand. Last ES-direct success: A **1000** flaps, B **2000** docs / 200 flaps |\n| **TOP zip** | ES\\|QL in ES | **span starts only** (no duration / end) | `TOP(@timestamp, 10000, \"asc\", \u2026)`, one expand. Cheaper; last ES-direct success: A **2000**, B **4000** / 400 |\n| **TOP zip + Kibana duration** (`top_zip_kibana_duration`) | Kibana HTTP probe | TOP zip starts, then Kibana attaches `duration_ms` / `status_ended_at` | Kibana reduce <10 ms; still dies at 10k on ES (`esql_block_factory`). Last HTTP success: **5k / 500** |\n| **search_after** | Query DSL PIT + Kibana RLE | full spans | page events (2000), run-length-encode in Kibana. Cheap through **10k events / 1k flaps** (~102 ms) |\n| **ES\\|QL + Kibana RLE** (`esql`) | one-shot ES\\|QL `KEEP`/`SORT`/`LIMIT 10000` + Kibana RLE | full spans | one ES\\|QL round-trip, same reducer as search_after. Assumes episode < 10k events |\n\nSeries like `A / top_zip` = Pattern A data + TOP zip query. `A / values_zip` = same A data, VALUES zip query.\n\n**Why A looks slower on TOP zip:** same `docs`, more span rows (every event is a transition). search_after tracks **docs**, not flaps, so A vs B at the same window is about the same.\n",
        "settings": {
          "open_links_in_new_tab": true
        }
      },
      "id": "legend-patterns-methods",
      "type": "markdown"
    },
